WEBVTT

00:00:00.056 --> 00:00:03.207
♪ “Stampede”
by Genesis Owusu ♪

00:00:03.207 --> 00:00:04.600
Once you've been to the moon...

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.793
♪

00:00:05.793 --> 00:00:07.128
[WHOOSHING]
...where do you go next?

00:00:07.128 --> 00:00:08.713
♪

00:00:08.713 --> 00:00:09.797
Back to work.

00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:11.667
♪

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.287
[CLICKING]

00:00:13.287 --> 00:00:15.136
♪

00:00:15.136 --> 00:00:16.721
You start with the chip.

00:00:16.721 --> 00:00:19.348
You engineer a new CPU core.

00:00:19.348 --> 00:00:21.851
You engineer a new GPU core.

00:00:21.851 --> 00:00:24.145
You add a second Neural Engine.

00:00:24.145 --> 00:00:26.522
Now you've just doubled
the compute power,

00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:29.484
pushed graphics
up to 40 per cent faster,

00:00:29.484 --> 00:00:32.320
unlocked Siri AI

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.239
and built the fastest chip
ever put in an iPhone.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:37.241
♪

00:00:37.241 --> 00:00:39.035
But there's a catch:

00:00:39.035 --> 00:00:41.245
More power creates more heat.

00:00:41.245 --> 00:00:44.499
So you give the vapour chamber
three times more surface area,

00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:47.794
because a bigger vapour chamber
cools the chip.

00:00:47.794 --> 00:00:51.087
A cooler chip creates
a more efficient chip.

00:00:51.104 --> 00:00:53.439
A more efficient chip
uses less battery.

00:00:53.439 --> 00:00:54.492
♪

00:00:54.492 --> 00:00:57.154
A battery that works less
lasts longer.

00:00:57.154 --> 00:00:58.942
♪

00:00:58.942 --> 00:01:00.987
The ultimate battery life.

00:01:00.987 --> 00:01:04.105
♪

00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:05.186
[CLICK]

00:01:05.186 --> 00:01:06.729
Next, you strengthen it...

00:01:06.729 --> 00:01:08.231
[CLICK]
[THUD]

00:01:08.231 --> 00:01:09.148
[HISSING]
...and test it...

00:01:09.148 --> 00:01:10.108
♪

00:01:10.108 --> 00:01:12.220
...for wherever you need
to take it.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.321
Then you ask, "What's next
for the camera system?"

00:01:15.321 --> 00:01:17.323
You want to improve
low-light photography

00:01:17.323 --> 00:01:19.617
and depth of field,
so you design

00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:22.203
and prototype
until you’ve just invented

00:01:22.203 --> 00:01:25.623
the first variable aperture
on an iPhone.

00:01:25.623 --> 00:01:27.125
♪

00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:29.502
A variable aperture
that automatically adjusts

00:01:29.502 --> 00:01:31.963
in any lighting condition,

00:01:31.963 --> 00:01:33.835
and improves sharpness
throughout a scene.

00:01:33.835 --> 00:01:34.882
[CAMERA SHUTTER]

00:01:34.882 --> 00:01:36.425
You also want
to give photographers

00:01:36.425 --> 00:01:38.344
more creative control.

00:01:38.344 --> 00:01:40.263
So you add pro controls,

00:01:40.263 --> 00:01:44.267
allowing them to quickly
set aperture, shutter speed

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:45.935
and the colour balance
of an image.

00:01:45.935 --> 00:01:46.936
[WAVES LAPPING]

00:01:46.936 --> 00:01:48.688
And because you have
the most powerful chip

00:01:48.688 --> 00:01:50.189
ever put in an iPhone...

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:51.399
♪

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:53.115
...you can push the camera
even further.

00:01:53.115 --> 00:01:54.819
[CAMERA SHUTTERS]

00:01:54.819 --> 00:01:57.958
You can shoot time-lapse in 4K
with high dynamic range.

00:01:57.958 --> 00:01:59.490
[WIND RUSHING]

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.118
You can apply Cinematic mode
to a regular video,

00:02:02.118 --> 00:02:04.025
even after you've shot it.

00:02:04.025 --> 00:02:06.706
♪

00:02:06.706 --> 00:02:09.000
You can customise
texture and grain

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.114
with Photographic Styles.

00:02:11.114 --> 00:02:14.689
[CAMERA SHUTTERS]

00:02:14.689 --> 00:02:16.507
[WHIRRING]

00:02:16.507 --> 00:02:19.177
Now you’ve just created
a camera system so intelligent

00:02:19.177 --> 00:02:22.638
and so capable that
photographers and filmmakers

00:02:22.638 --> 00:02:25.089
can reach new levels
of creativity.

00:02:25.089 --> 00:02:26.303
♪

00:02:26.303 --> 00:02:27.970
[WAVES CRASHING]

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:29.377
♪

00:02:29.377 --> 00:02:30.247
[MECHANICAL WHIRRING]

00:02:30.247 --> 00:02:34.942
♪

00:02:34.942 --> 00:02:38.863
A chip built for AI
that runs faster than ever.

00:02:38.863 --> 00:02:41.574
A battery that lasts
longer than ever.

00:02:41.574 --> 00:02:45.161
The most intelligent
pro camera system ever.

00:02:45.161 --> 00:02:47.496
This is what happens
when you go to the moon,

00:02:47.496 --> 00:02:50.091
come back and ask,
“What’s next?”

00:02:50.091 --> 00:02:52.211
♪

